For Forsaken Linux Lite this was easy by typing doas setup-desktop
NOTE FOR FORSAKEN LINUX LITE: The Desktop Environment and Window Managers Are Limited

For TTY Login auto startx when after login

If you want startx to run automatically every time you log into the first terminal (tty1), add this snippet to your shell's profile file (like ~/.bash_profile or ~/.zprofile)

if [[ -z $DISPLAY && $XDG_VTNR -eq 1 ]]; then
    exec startx
fi

NOTE: FORSAKEN LINUX 16-BIT IS NOT SUPPORTED BECAUSE ITS ELKS BASED

Forsaken Linux wont Recommend You to Install GNOME or KDE Plasma in Virtual Machine because it ended up crash the vm example Oracle VirtualBox Stopped Due to Using a lot of memory.
GNOME and KDE are Heavy so it require more space because it its low storage you might be ended up by pacman saying not enough space. plus you need more Enough Memory For GNOME and KDE
If you managed to install GNOME and KDE in Virtualbox you might encounter slow performance and errors
